{"name":"Christmas Naanwidge","permalink":"christmas-naanwidge","edit":"https://github.com/The-Silverwood-Institute/Recibase/tree/master/src/main/scala/se/reciba/api/recibase/recipes/ChristmasNaanwidge.scala","source":"Gousto","description":null,"tagline":null,"notes":[],"dated_notes":[],"tags":["Stodge","Vegetarian","Spicy","Christmas","AI"],"inherited_tags":["Vegetarian-ish","Pescatarian"],"image":null,"ingredients_blocks":[{"name":null,"ingredients":[{"name":"Coriander","quantity":"10g","prep":null,"notes":null},{"name":"Ground turmeric","quantity":"1 tsp","prep":null,"notes":null},{"name":"Dried chilli flakes","quantity":"1/2 tsp","prep":null,"notes":null},{"name":"Curry powder","quantity":"1 tbsp","prep":null,"notes":null},{"name":"Carrot","quantity":"1","prep":"grated","notes":null},{"name":"Parsnip","quantity":"1","prep":"peeled into ribbons","notes":null},{"name":"Potatoes","quantity":"3","prep":"peeled and diced into small cubes","notes":null},{"name":"Paneer","quantity":"200g","prep":"chopped into cubes","notes":null},{"name":"Greek-style yoghurt","quantity":"100g","prep":null,"notes":null},{"name":"Smoked paprika","quantity":"1 tsp","prep":null,"notes":null},{"name":"Cranberry sauce","quantity":"40g","prep":null,"notes":null},{"name":"Tamarind paste","quantity":"15g","prep":null,"notes":null},{"name":"Plain naans","quantity":"2","prep":null,"notes":null},{"name":"Salt","quantity":null,"prep":null,"notes":null},{"name":"Pepper","quantity":null,"prep":null,"notes":null},{"name":"Oil","quantity":null,"prep":null,"notes":null}]}],"method":["Preheat the oven to 220°C (fan 200°C).","Add the diced potatoes to one side of a baking tray and sprinkle with half the curry powder, season with a pinch of salt and pepper and drizzle with vegetable oil.","Give everything a good mix up and put the tray in the oven for an initial 6-8 min.","Stir together the ground turmeric, smoked paprika and chilli flakes in a large bowl with the remaining curry powder, half the Greek-style yoghurt and a pinch of salt and pepper.","Add the chopped paneer to the tandoori marinade and give everything a good mix up.","After the potatoes have had their initial 6-8 min, add the tandoori paneer to the other side of the baking tray.","Return the tray to the oven and cook for a further 10-12 min or until golden and soft.","Combine the cranberry sauce, tamarind paste and grated carrot in a bowl to make tamarind & cranberry slaw.","Chop the coriander finely, including the stalks (saving a few whole leaves to garnish).","Once the golden tandoori paneer is cooked, transfer it to a clean chopping board and reserve the tray.","Add the parsnip ribbons to the reserved tray and return it to the oven for 5 min further or until both the potatoes and parsnips are golden and crispy.","Put the plain naans in the oven for 3 min or until warmed through.","Spread the remaining Greek-style yoghurt over naan, then top with the tamarind & cranberry slaw and the golden tandoori paneer.","Sprinkle over the chopped coriander and top with the remaining naan.","Cut each naanwich into 4 and garnish with the reserved coriander leaves and crispy parsnip ribbons.","Serve with the spiced roast potatoes to the side."]}